---
import WorkbenchLayout from "../../../layouts/WorkbenchLayout.astro";

const protocolText = `AI Input Check Protocol

Review the following input for missing or ambiguous criteria that could force an AI system to guess.

Do not rewrite the input.
Do not solve the task.
Do not improve style.
Do not infer hidden intent.
Do not assume business context.
Do not assume authority.
Do not assume risk tolerance.
Do not assume the desired outcome beyond what the input states.

Only identify what is missing, unclear, ambiguous, conflicting, unstated, undefined, incomplete, or implied.

First, identify the following only if they are present in the input:
- actor
- trigger
- action
- outcome
- scope
- constraint
- dependency
- sequence

If an element is not present, write:
- [element]&#58; not specified

Then identify gaps using only this diagnostic vocabulary.

Elements:
- actor
- trigger
- action
- outcome
- scope
- constraint
- dependency
- sequence

Gap types:
- missing
- unclear
- ambiguous
- unstated
- undefined
- conflicting
- incomplete
- implied

Rules for findings:
- Express every finding as: [gap type] [element]
- Do not invent new labels
- Do not use synonyms
- Do not explain with long paragraphs
- Keep findings short and literal
- List only meaningful gaps that could change interpretation, behavior, or output
- If the input would require the AI system to guess, mark the relevant element as not specified or as a detected gap
- Every Detected Gap must use only one allowed gap type and one allowed element
- Do not create new elements such as audience, channel, sender, recipient, tone, service details, format, or booking method
- If a missing detail does not fit the allowed element list, map it to the nearest allowed element or omit it

Return results in exactly this format:

Input Summary
- actor: ...
- trigger: ...
- action: ...
- outcome: ...
- scope: ...
- constraint: ...
- dependency: ...
- sequence: ...

Detected Gaps
- ...
- ...
- ...

Now review this input:

[PASTE INPUT HERE]`;

const elements = [
  "actor",
  "trigger",
  "action",
  "outcome",
  "scope",
  "constraint",
  "dependency",
  "sequence",
];

const gapTypes = [
  "missing",
  "unclear",
  "ambiguous",
  "unstated",
  "undefined",
  "conflicting",
  "incomplete",
  "implied",
];
---

<WorkbenchLayout
  title="Check Input | PENGO Workbench"
  description="A copyable protocol for inspecting what an AI ask leaves open for the model to guess."
  url="https://pengosystems.com/workbench/check-input/"
  active="check-inputs"
  breadcrumb="Check Input"
>
  <article class="wb-content wb-template">
    <div class="wb-page-action">
      <span aria-current="page">Check Input</span>
      <a href="/workbench/explore-results/">Explore Results</a>
    </div>

    <p class="wb-type-label">Input Inspection</p>
    <h1>Check Input</h1>
    <p class="wb-lede">
      Stop guessing. Narrow the ask.
    </p>

    <section class="wb-reading-section">
      <h2>What It Is</h2>
      <p>
        Check Input is a public protocol for inspecting an AI ask before blaming the model.
        It helps identify what the input left missing, unclear, implied, conflicting, or unstated.
      </p>
      <p>
        Use the protocol with any AI system. It should return an Input Summary and a Detected Gaps list using controlled terms.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="wb-reading-section">
      <h2>What It Does</h2>
      <p>
        Check Input helps you inspect the original ask and identify what it forced the AI system to guess.
      </p>
      <p>
        After the AI returns an Input Summary and Detected Gaps, bring that output back to PENGO and map it into the Workbench.
      </p>
      <p class="wb-next-link">
        <a href="/workbench/explore-results/">Open Explore Results</a>
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="wb-reading-section">
      <h2>What It Does Not Do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>It does not diagnose the model.</li>
        <li>It does not prove causality.</li>
        <li>It does not validate correctness.</li>
        <li>It does not classify a failure.</li>
        <li>It does not produce receipts.</li>
        <li>It does not replace DIVU.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="wb-reading-section">
      <h2>Copyable Protocol</h2>
      <p>
        Copy this protocol and paste it into an AI system with the input you want inspected.
      </p>

      <div class="wb-copy-panel">
        <div class="wb-copy-panel__bar">
          <p>AI Input Check Protocol</p>
          <button type="button" data-copy-protocol>Copy</button>
        </div>

        <textarea readonly rows="28" data-protocol-text>{protocolText}</textarea>
      </div>

      <p>
        After the AI returns an Input Summary and Detected Gaps, bring the output back to PENGO and use Explore Results to map it into related Patterns and useful Lenses.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="wb-reading-section">
      <h2>Controlled Vocabulary</h2>

      <h3>Elements</h3>
      <ul>
        {elements.map((element) => (
          <li>{element}</li>
        ))}
      </ul>

      <h3>Gap Types</h3>
      <ul>
        {gapTypes.map((gapType) => (
          <li>{gapType}</li>
        ))}
      </ul>

      <p>
        Every finding should use this shape: <code>[gap type] [element]</code>.
      </p>

      <p>
        Examples:
        <code>missing actor</code>,
        <code>unclear scope</code>,
        <code>unstated constraint</code>.
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li><strong>missing actor</strong> = who is responsible, affected, addressed, or expected to act is not named.</li>
        <li><strong>unclear scope</strong> = where the request applies or stops is not clear.</li>
        <li><strong>unstated constraint</strong> = a rule, limit, requirement, or exclusion is assumed but not said.</li>
      </ul>

      <p class="wb-next-link">
        <a href="/workbench/check-input/gap-examples/">See all Gap Examples</a>
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="wb-reading-section">
      <h2>Example Output</h2>

      <pre><code>{`Input Summary
- actor: not specified
- trigger: not specified
- action: write a refund email
- outcome: not specified
- scope: unclear
- constraint: not specified
- dependency: refund policy not specified
- sequence: not specified

Detected Gaps
- missing actor
- unstated outcome
- unclear scope
- unstated constraint
- missing dependency`}</code></pre>
    </section>

    <section class="wb-reading-section">
      <h2>Boundary</h2>
      <p>
        Check Input surfaces controlled gap terms. These terms can help surface related Patterns and useful Lenses, but they are related structural references, not a final diagnosis.
      </p>
      <p>
        Check Input turns an AI problem back toward the ask.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>

<style>
  .wb-copy-panel {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 18px;
    background: var(--color-surface);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .wb-copy-panel__bar {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: 0.75rem 0.9rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .wb-copy-panel__bar p {
    margin: 0 !important;
    color: var(--color-text) !important;
    font-size: 0.82rem !important;
    line-height: 1.1 !important;
    font-weight: 850 !important;
  }

  .wb-copy-panel__bar button {
    appearance: none;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-accent);
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    padding: 0.42rem 0.75rem;
    font: inherit;
    font-size: 0.74rem;
    line-height: 1;
    font-weight: 900;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .wb-copy-panel__bar button:hover {
    background: var(--color-accent);
    color: var(--color-bg);
  }

  .wb-copy-panel textarea {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    min-height: 34rem;
    padding: 1rem;
    border: 0;
    resize: vertical;
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--color-text);
    font: 0.82rem/1.55 ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Monaco, Consolas, "Liberation Mono", "Courier New", monospace;
    white-space: pre;
  }

  .wb-copy-panel textarea:focus {
    outline: 2px solid var(--color-accent);
    outline-offset: -2px;
  }
</style>

<script>
  const copyButton = document.querySelector("[data-copy-protocol]");
  const protocolTextArea = document.querySelector("[data-protocol-text]");

  copyButton?.addEventListener("click", async () => {
    if (!(protocolTextArea instanceof HTMLTextAreaElement)) return;

    try {
      await navigator.clipboard.writeText(protocolTextArea.value);
      copyButton.textContent = "Copied";
      window.setTimeout(() => {
        copyButton.textContent = "Copy";
      }, 1600);
    } catch {
      protocolTextArea.focus();
      protocolTextArea.select();
      document.execCommand("copy");
      copyButton.textContent = "Copied";
      window.setTimeout(() => {
        copyButton.textContent = "Copy";
      }, 1600);
    }
  });
</script>
\n</WorkbenchLayout>
